# Singapore family and succession — whole families, carried through all four Acts

## What this corpus can and cannot say

<!-- l4: declare:What this corpus can say about the distribution of an estate -->

**1.** In this Act, “What this corpus can say about the distribution of an estate” means one of the following—

    (a) “the Intestate Succession Act 1967 governs the distribution, and its rules have been applied”;

    (b) “nothing in the Intestate Succession Act 1967 applies to this estate, and no other Act in this corpus distributes it”;

    (c) “the Intestate Succession Act 1967 applies to the estate but has no effect on these facts”;

    (d) “the deceased was domiciled outside Singapore and left no immovable property here, so section 4(1) sends the distribution of his movable property to the law of his domicile, and no Act in this corpus is that law”;

    (e) “the deceased was domiciled in Singapore and was possessed beneficially of no property situated here, so section 4(1) names the law of Singapore and section 5 reaches no property to distribute”; or

    (f) “the death is not proved to be after 2 June 1967, so section 5 does not reach this estate, and no other Act in this corpus distributes it”.

<!-- l4: decide:what this corpus can say about the distribution of the estate -->

**2.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, what this corpus can say about the distribution of the estate means if not this Act applies to the estate with the deceased person then nothing in the Intestate Succession Act 1967 applies to this estate, and no other Act in this corpus distributes it if this Act has effect in respect of the estate with the deceased person then the Intestate Succession Act 1967 governs the distribution, and its rules have been applied if not section 3 — an “intestate” within the meaning of this Act with the deceased person then the Intestate Succession Act 1967 applies to the estate but has no effect on these facts if not section 5 — the person dies intestate after 2 June 1967 with the deceased person then the death is not proved to be after 2 June 1967, so section 5 does not reach this estate, and no other Act in this corpus distributes it if not section 5(a) — domiciled in Singapore and possessed beneficially of property situated in Singapore with the deceased person or section 5(b) — domiciled outside Singapore and possessed beneficially of immovable property situated in Singapore with the deceased person and not section 4(1) — the law of the country of domicile is the law of Singapore with the deceased person then the deceased was domiciled outside Singapore and left no immovable property here, so section 4(1) sends the distribution of his movable property to the law of his domicile, and no Act in this corpus is that law if not section 5(a) — domiciled in Singapore and possessed beneficially of property situated in Singapore with the deceased person or section 5(b) — domiciled outside Singapore and possessed beneficially of immovable property situated in Singapore with the deceased person and section 4(1) — the law of the country of domicile is the law of Singapore with the deceased person then the deceased was domiciled in Singapore and was possessed beneficially of no property situated here, so section 4(1) names the law of Singapore and section 5 reaches no property to distribute otherwise the Intestate Succession Act 1967 applies to the estate but has no effect on these facts.

<!-- l4: decide:the guardians the Guardianship of Infants Act counts, for whom the case file holds a record -->

**3.** In relation to an Infant “the infant concerned in the estate”, the guardians the Guardianship of Infants Act counts, for whom the case file holds a record means filter with given the guardian then elem with the reference for the guardian with the guardian and the persons who are guardians of the infant with the infant concerned in the estate and the infant concerned in the estate's the guardians of the infant.

<!-- l4: decide:the guardians the Guardianship of Infants Act counts, for whom the case file holds no record -->

**4.** In relation to an Infant “the infant concerned in the estate”, the guardians the Guardianship of Infants Act counts, for whom the case file holds no record means filter with given the reference then not elem with the reference and map with the reference for the guardian and the infant concerned in the estate's the guardians of the infant and the persons who are guardians of the infant with the infant concerned in the estate.

<!-- l4: declare:Whether a guardian could give a good discharge for the infant’s share -->

**5.** In this Act, “Whether a guardian could give a good discharge for the infant’s share” means one of the following—

    (a) “a guardian whom the Guardianship of Infants Act counts could give a good discharge for the infant’s share”;

    (b) “no guardian whom the Guardianship of Infants Act counts could give a good discharge for the infant’s share”; or

    (c) “the Guardianship of Infants Act counts as guardian a person for whom the case file records no kind of guardianship, so section 17 cannot be asked about him”.

<!-- l4: decide:whether some guardian of this infant could give a good discharge for the infant’s share -->

**6.** In relation to an Infant “the infant concerned in the estate”, whether some guardian of this infant could give a good discharge for the infant’s share means if any with given the guardian then not section 17 denies the guardian power to give a good discharge with the guardian and the guardians the Guardianship of Infants Act counts, for whom the case file holds a record with the infant concerned in the estate then a guardian whom the Guardianship of Infants Act counts could give a good discharge for the infant’s share if not null with the guardians the Guardianship of Infants Act counts, for whom the case file holds no record with the infant concerned in the estate then the Guardianship of Infants Act counts as guardian a person for whom the case file records no kind of guardianship, so section 17 cannot be asked about him otherwise no guardian whom the Guardianship of Infants Act counts could give a good discharge for the infant’s share.

## Constructors — one record, four Acts

<!-- l4: decide:a person in the case file, in full -->

**7.** In relation to a STRING “the name of the person”, a STRING “the reference”, an optional DATE “when he was born”, an optional DATE “when he attains the age of majority”, a Vital status “whether he is living”, a list of Child “his children”, a BOOLEAN “he is a soldier being in actual military service”, a BOOLEAN “he is a mariner or seaman being at sea”, a BOOLEAN “he is so circumstanced”, a BOOLEAN “he lacks mental capacity”, a BOOLEAN “he is absent from Singapore”, a BOOLEAN “he is willing to act” and a BOOLEAN “he so desires”, a person in the case file, in full means Person where name is the name of the person, the reference for this person is the reference, date of birth is when he was born, vital status is whether he is living, children is his children, at the date of the death only conceived in the womb but subsequently born alive is FALSE, money or other property given, paid or settled by the intestate during his life to or for the advancement of the person is 0, the date on which the person attains the age of majority is when he attains the age of majority, a soldier being in actual military service is he is a soldier being in actual military service, a mariner or seaman being at sea is he is a mariner or seaman being at sea, a member of any naval or marine forces so circumstanced that if he were a soldier he would be in actual military service is he is so circumstanced, so desires that letters of administration be granted to such person as the court thinks fit is he so desires, lacks mental capacity (within the meaning of the Mental Capacity Act 2008) to make decisions with respect to the management and administration of the person's property and affairs is he lacks mental capacity, absent from Singapore is he is absent from Singapore and willing to act is he is willing to act.

<!-- l4: decide:a person in the case file -->

**8.** In relation to a STRING “the name of the person”, a STRING “the reference”, an optional DATE “when he was born”, an optional DATE “when he attains the age of majority”, a Vital status “whether he is living” and a list of Child “his children”, a person in the case file means a person in the case file, in full with the name of the person, the reference, when he was born, when he attains the age of majority, whether he is living, his children, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:twenty-one years after -->

**9.** In relation to a DATE “when he was born”, twenty-one years after means JUST with Date with DATE_DAY with when he was born, DATE_MONTH with when he was born and the sum of DATE_YEAR with when he was born and 21.

<!-- l4: decide:a legitimate child in the case file -->

**10.** In relation to a Person “the offspring”, a legitimate child in the case file means Child where the child is the offspring, a legitimate child of the person whose child he is is TRUE and adopted by that person by virtue of an order of court under any written law for the time being in force in Singapore, Malaysia or Brunei Darussalam is FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:a child in the case file neither legitimate nor adopted -->

**11.** In relation to a Person “the offspring”, a child in the case file neither legitimate nor adopted means Child where the child is the offspring, a legitimate child of the person whose child he is is FALSE and adopted by that person by virtue of an order of court under any written law for the time being in force in Singapore, Malaysia or Brunei Darussalam is FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:a marriage in the case file -->

**12.** In relation to a Person “the other party”, an optional DATE “when it was solemnised” and a BOOLEAN “it subsists”, a marriage in the case file means Marriage where the spouse is the other party, the date of the solemnisation of the marriage is when it was solemnised and subsisting at the death of the deceased, in the sense of not dissolved or annulled before the death is it subsists.

<!-- l4: decide:a family in the case file -->

**13.** In relation to a list of Marriage “the marriages”, an optional Person “the father” and an optional Person “the mother”, a family in the case file means Family where the marriages of the deceased is the marriages, the father of the deceased is the father, the mother of the deceased is the mother, the brothers and sisters of the deceased is EMPTY, the grandparents of the deceased is EMPTY and the uncles and aunts of the deceased is EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:an estate in the case file, with creditors -->

**14.** In relation to a Money “movable property in Singapore”, a Money “immovable property in Singapore”, a Money “the expenses of due administration”, a Money “the debts and liabilities”, a Money “the value beneficially disposed of by the will” and a list of Creditor “the creditors”, an estate in the case file, with creditors means Estate where the value of the movable property situated in Singapore is movable property in Singapore, the value of the immovable property situated in Singapore is immovable property in Singapore, the value of the movable property situated outside Singapore is 0, the value of the immovable property situated outside Singapore is 0, the value of any property which the deceased possessed or was entitled to as trustee and not beneficially, situated in Singapore is 0, the value of any property which the deceased possessed or was entitled to as trustee and not beneficially, situated outside Singapore is 0, the value of any moneys payable by an appointed insurer pursuant to the Dependants’ Protection Insurance Scheme or any other equivalent scheme maintained by the Central Provident Fund Board is 0, the value of the property administered by the Public Trustee is 0, the amount of the funds in court directed to be paid, transferred or delivered to him is 0, the value of land settled previously to the death of the deceased is 0, the trustees of the settlement is EMPTY, the value of the interest in property which at the time of his death is charged with the payment of money is 0, the amount of the charge on that interest is 0, the deceased has by will, deed or other document signified a contrary or other intention is FALSE, the debts and liabilities of the deceased is the debts and liabilities, the funeral, testamentary and administration expenses is the expenses of due administration, the creditors of the deceased is the creditors, fully administered is FALSE and the value of the property beneficially disposed of by the will is the value beneficially disposed of by the will.

