**18.** In relation to a Person “the appointee”, a STRING “the reference for the infant”, a How the guardian was appointed “how he was appointed” and a Kind of guardianship “of the person or of the property”, a guardian in the case file whom the surviving parent objects to means Guardian where the guardian is the appointee, the reference for the infant is the reference for the infant, how the guardian was appointed is how he was appointed, of the person or of the property is of the person or of the property, alone or jointly is alone, refuses to act is FALSE, the mother or father objects to his so acting is TRUE, considers that the mother or father is unfit to have the custody of the infant is FALSE, removed from his guardianship by the court is FALSE, has given security is TRUE, the court has otherwise ordered as to security is FALSE, has sold, mortgaged, exchanged, or otherwise parted with the possession of any of the movable or immovable property of the infant is FALSE, has leased land belonging to the infant is FALSE, the term of the lease, in years is NOTHING, has the permission of the court to deal with the property of the infant is FALSE, has given a good discharge for a legacy or other capital moneys payable to or receivable by the infant is FALSE, the court has otherwise ordered as to giving a good discharge is FALSE, the provision made out of the income of the property of the infant for his maintenance and education is A periodical sum where the sum is 0 and the period is monthly and has the permission of the court to apply a sum exceeding $100 per month is FALSE.

