**22.** In relation to a Person “the person who died”, a Family “his family”, an Estate “his estate”, an optional Will “his will”, a BOOLEAN “he was a Muslim”, a BOOLEAN “he was domiciled in Singapore”, a list of Grant “the grants” and a list of Infant “the infants concerned in the estate”, a deceased person in the case file, in full means Deceased person where the deceased is the person who died, the family is his family, the estate is his estate, the will is his will, domiciled in Singapore at the time of his death is he was domiciled in Singapore, carried on business or resided in Singapore within 12 months of his death is TRUE, a Muslim is he was a Muslim, the grants made in respect of the estate is the grants, the probate applications made in respect of the estate is EMPTY, a next of kin, creditor or other person has appeared and made out a claim to letters of administration is FALSE and the infants concerned in the estate is the infants concerned in the estate.

