## The joins, as expressions

<!-- l4: decide:the capital moneys of this infant that no guardian may give a good discharge for -->

**27.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person” and an Infant “the infant concerned in the estate”, the capital moneys of this infant that no guardian may give a good discharge for means if whether some guardian of this infant could give a good discharge for the infant’s share with the infant concerned in the estate is equal to a guardian whom the Guardianship of Infants Act counts could give a good discharge for the infant’s share, then 0; otherwise, the sum taken under the Intestate Succession Act by the person whose reference is with the deceased person and the infant concerned in the estate's the infant's the reference for this person.

