**28.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person” and a Grantee “the grantee”, the Guardianship of Infants Act counts this grantee as a guardian of the infant for whose use the grant is made means consider the case distinctions of the grantee's the reference for the person for whose use and benefit the grant is made :  when NOTHING has  then FALSE. when JUST has the reference for the infant then any with given the infant then the infant's the infant's the reference for this person is equal to the reference for the infant and any with given the reference for a guardian then _ is the individual whose reference is _ with the grantee's the grantee and the reference for a guardian and the persons who are guardians of the infant with the infant and the deceased person's the infants concerned in the estate.

<!-- l4: decide:the grantees taking as the guardian of the person and property of the infant -->

**29.** In relation to a Grant “the grant”, the grantees taking as the guardian of the person and property of the infant means filter with given the grantee then the grantee's the capacity in which the grant is made is equal to as the guardian of the person and property of the infant and the grant's the grantees.

<!-- l4: declare:Whether section 21(2) and the Guardianship of Infants Act agree about this grant -->

**30.** In this Act, “Whether section 21(2) and the Guardianship of Infants Act agree about this grant” means one of the following—

    (a) “both Acts are satisfied: the Probate Act opens section 21(2) and the Guardianship of Infants Act counts the grantee as a guardian of the infant”;

    (b) “the Probate and Administration Act opens section 21(2) on this grant, and the Guardianship of Infants Act does not count the grantee as a guardian of the infant”;

    (c) “the Guardianship of Infants Act counts the grantee as a guardian of the infant, and the Probate and Administration Act does not open section 21(2) on this grant”; or

    (d) “neither Act is satisfied on this grant”.

<!-- l4: decide:whether section 21(2) and the Guardianship of Infants Act agree about this grant -->

**31.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, a Grant “the grant” and a DATE “the date”, whether section 21(2) and the Guardianship of Infants Act agree about this grant means if s 21(2) — letters of administration may be granted to the guardian of the person and property of the infant with the deceased person, the grant and the date and the Guardianship Act counts every grantee taking as guardian then both Acts are satisfied: the Probate Act opens section 21(2) and the Guardianship of Infants Act counts the grantee as a guardian of the infant if s 21(2) — letters of administration may be granted to the guardian of the person and property of the infant with the deceased person, the grant and the date then the Probate and Administration Act opens section 21(2) on this grant, and the Guardianship of Infants Act does not count the grantee as a guardian of the infant if the Guardianship Act counts every grantee taking as guardian then the Guardianship of Infants Act counts the grantee as a guardian of the infant, and the Probate and Administration Act does not open section 21(2) on this grant otherwise neither Act is satisfied on this grant.

For the purposes of this provision—

“the Guardianship Act counts every grantee taking as guardian” means not null with the grantees taking as the guardian of the person and property of the infant with the grant and all with given the grantee then the Guardianship of Infants Act counts this grantee as a guardian of the infant for whose use the grant is made with the deceased person and the grantee and the grantees taking as the guardian of the person and property of the infant with the grant;

<!-- l4: decide:the guardian holds under an appointment made by a parent by will -->

**32.** In relation to a Guardian “the guardian”, the guardian holds under an appointment made by a parent by will means consider the case distinctions of the guardian's how the guardian was appointed :  when appointed by the father by will has  then TRUE. when appointed by the mother by will has  then TRUE. in any other case FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:every testamentary guardian the Guardianship of Infants Act counts holds under an appointment the Wills Act has made good -->

**33.** In relation to an A case under this Act “the will, put to the Wills Act” and an Infant “the infant concerned in the estate”, every testamentary guardian the Guardianship of Infants Act counts holds under an appointment the Wills Act has made good means all with given the guardian then elem with the reference for the guardian with the guardian and the references for the guardians whose appointment this Act has made good with the will, put to the Wills Act and filter with the guardian holds under an appointment made by a parent by will and the guardians the Guardianship of Infants Act counts, for whom the case file holds a record with the infant concerned in the estate.

<!-- l4: decide:the Wills Act leaves this will operative -->

**34.** In relation to an A case under this Act “the will, put to the Wills Act”, the Wills Act leaves this will operative if—

    (a) any of the following applies—

        (i) the formal validity of the will with the will, put to the Wills Act is equal to valid; or

        (ii) the formal validity of the will with the will, put to the Wills Act is equal to valid, being the will of a soldier being in actual military service, or of a mariner or seaman being at sea, disposing of his personal estate (section 27(1)); and

    (b) s 15 — the will does not have been revoked with the will, put to the Wills Act.

<!-- l4: declare:Whether the case file agrees with the Wills Act about the will -->

**35.** In this Act, “Whether the case file agrees with the Wills Act about the will” means one of the following—

    (a) “the Wills Act leaves this will operative, and the case file holds it”;

    (b) “the Wills Act leaves no operative will, and the case file has struck it out”;

    (c) “the Wills Act leaves no operative will, and the case file still holds it, so the other three Acts answer as though it stood”; or

    (d) “the Wills Act leaves this will operative, and the case file has struck it out, so the other three Acts answer as though there were none”.

<!-- l4: decide:whether the case file agrees with the Wills Act about the will -->

**36.** In relation to a Deceased person “the case file” and an A case under this Act “the will, put to the Wills Act”, whether the case file agrees with the Wills Act about the will means if the Wills Act leaves this will operative with the will, put to the Wills Act and isJust with the case file's the will then the Wills Act leaves this will operative, and the case file holds it if the Wills Act leaves this will operative with the will, put to the Wills Act then the Wills Act leaves this will operative, and the case file has struck it out, so the other three Acts answer as though there were none if isJust with the case file's the will then the Wills Act leaves no operative will, and the case file still holds it, so the other three Acts answer as though it stood otherwise the Wills Act leaves no operative will, and the case file has struck it out.

<!-- l4: decide:the Wills Act has left no operative will and the Intestate Succession Act still reads one -->

**37.** In relation to a Deceased person “the case file” and an A case under this Act “the will, put to the Wills Act”, the Wills Act has left no operative will and the Intestate Succession Act still reads one if—

    (a) it is not the case that the Wills Act leaves this will operative with the will, put to the Wills Act; and

    (b) it is not the case that section 3 — an “intestate” within the meaning of this Act with the case file.

<!-- l4: decide:the Wills Act has left no operative will and the Probate Act still routes to probate -->

**38.** In relation to a Deceased person “the case file” and an A case under this Act “the will, put to the Wills Act”, the Wills Act has left no operative will and the Probate Act still routes to probate if—

    (a) it is not the case that the Wills Act leaves this will operative with the will, put to the Wills Act; and

    (b) s 18(1) — the person does not have died intestate with the case file.

<!-- l4: decide:the further facts, the section 29(5) antecedent taken from the Intestate Succession Act -->

**39.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, the further facts, the section 29(5) antecedent taken from the Intestate Succession Act means The further facts on which the grant machinery turns where the administrator is entitled to the whole of the estate after payment of the debts is one person takes the whole of the property distributable under this Act with the deceased person, the Family Court thinks fit to require such security is FALSE, there is danger that the property may be wasted is FALSE, it appears that such appointment would not be a sufficient protection for the estate is FALSE and the Public Trustee has by writing signed by him declared that he undertakes to administer such property is FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:the two Acts agree whether this person is an infant on this date -->

**40.** In relation to a Person “the person” and a DATE “the date”, the two Acts agree whether this person is an infant on this date means the person is an infant on the date in question with the person and the date is equal to JUST with _ is an infant on _ with the person and the date.

<!-- l4: decide:the two modules agree whether this child is a “child” within the meaning of section 3 -->

**41.** In relation to a Child “the relation”, the two modules agree whether this child is a “child” within the meaning of section 3 means section 3 — a “child” within the meaning of this Act with the relation is equal to a “child” within the meaning of section 3 of the Intestate Succession Act 1967 with the relation.

<!-- l4: decide:the two modules agree about every child of this deceased -->

**42.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, the two modules agree about every child of this deceased means all with the two modules agree whether this child is a “child” within the meaning of section 3 and the deceased person's the deceased's children.

# Scenario 1 — the intestacy with an infant child

## Scenario 1 — the people, the estate and the grant

<!-- l4: decide:the day letters of administration are applied for -->

**43.** The day letters of administration are applied for means YMD with 2026, 1 and 15.

<!-- l4: decide:Meera Sivakumar -->

**44.** Meera Sivakumar means a person in the case file with Meera Sivakumar, meera, JUST with YMD with 1968, 7 and 22, twenty-one years after with YMD with 1968, 7 and 22, living and EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:Arjun Sivakumar -->

**45.** Arjun Sivakumar means a person in the case file with Arjun Sivakumar, arjun, JUST with YMD with 2000, 4 and 10, twenty-one years after with YMD with 2000, 4 and 10, living and EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:Divya Sivakumar -->

